column14:
next checkpoint with the account team scheduled for the week of Aug/04 in respect to the teams priorities of quarter closure week;


 we had a quick alignment with part of the account team and introduced, at least very briefly, how our team might support up ahead, through some periodic syncs to help on the consumption related aspects, ensuring client is successful in their post-sales environment;


 we provided support for this account in the past in regards to the their expected migration [CDP to Consumption];
 we supported the account team in analysing and determining the consumption baseline, also considering some discounts applying on Internal Data Pipeline, which could should affect projections back then with the ratecards being updated;

Preparing the Data Cloud Consumption Session
 @Tarik den Boer and @Roelof van Wees provided guidance to @Vishal Patel on the key topics to cover in the Data Cloud consumption session, including the importance of explaining the unstructured data retrieval mechanisms. @Vishal Patel prepared example calculations to demonstrate the cost-effectiveness of the Data Cloud usage.


 Finalizing the Data Cloud Consumption Session
 @Vishal Patel finalized the presentation materials for the Data Cloud consumption session, incorporating feedback from @Nils Polano and @Tarik den Boer. @Roelof van Wees confirmed @Vishal Patel's time slot and logistics for the workshop.

