column14:
we provided a session to explain how the consumption model works, dedicated to to some of the key clients stakeholders, who were unaware of it.


 given that the SI partner is reportedly knowledgable in Marketing Cloud, we asked the SI partner for a mapping / list of their current MC use-cases so we could help brainstorm other MC use-cases, leveraging Data Cloud as segmentation mean, driving consumption; we'll continue to follow up on this as an attempt to help them grow consumption with relevance;


 Despite having a Data Cloud use-case implemented towards Service cloud, this client is reportedly using multiple Marketing Cloud journeys, however, they were historically not segmenting them through Data Cloud, instead, straight into MC; through our meetings, we have been evangelizing the benefits and importance of leveraging Data Cloud for segmenting its future MC journeys, not only to have faster segmentation (TTM: Time To Market) but also to be able to profit out of such data in Agentforce, which they might start using soon; they understood the idea of "if you bring data to Data Cloud, then you can leverage it both in Marketing Cloud, Service Cloud and Agentforce, so this is the most possible future-proof recommended architecture";

we had a strategy alignment with the AEs and offered 2 scenarios, in terms of projection of segmentation credit consumption optimization:
 conservative (54%) and aggressive (81%); the AEs remain thankful to our team's contribution;
 the current understanding is that, if the client follows as much of our recommendations as expected, they shall obtain an optimization of 80% of their current segmentation credit, making their migration [CDP to Consumption] more viable;
 good news: we already have data-based results (concrete data monitoring ) that the client has been following our recommendations;


 the client is about to go through a [CDP to Consumption] contract negotiation and migration / upgrade;
 (given the ad-hoc importance of this client, our team select it for a special and long-term work;)
 our goal has been: help maximize feasibility of the migration [CDP to Consumption] by deeply investigating backstage processing (consumption audit), throughout weeks / months, in order to provide a list of recommendations which the client could execute, performing a deep cleanup in their tech environment, reducing unnecessary processing, eliminating de-optimized credit consumption (prior to their migration), ensuring conditions for a smooth and successful migration;

Customer is live with AF e DC. Live with agent Moky (lavazza.it) on product recommendation, where is my order.
 API custom live on IT, UK, then FR and Australia. Once stabilized they will scale up with telemetry data and agent with proactive reachout. 
 CL intro to customer- Next steps: plan periodic consumption review; plan again a consumption model session; help estimate telemetry use case;

we had a 1st round of sync with the 2 key members of the account team;


 first impressions (TBC):
 - it seems that the client is not getting the implementation progressing as desired;
 - the root-cause seems to be that the SI partner might be lacking the proper familiarity with the DC product, consumption model, trying to implement too many things in a single implementation (waterfall) instead of prioritizing 1 use-case at time;
